    "# Lab 5: Building ETL Pipelines using PySpark\n",
    "## Course: Data Stores & Pipelines (Trimester 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to Lab 5! In this worked example, we will design and execute an end-to-end **ETL (Extract, Transform, Load)** pipeline using **PySpark**. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Learning Objectives:\n",
    "* **Extract:** Initialize a `SparkSession` and ingest raw datasets.\n",
    "* **Transform:** Clean data, handle missing values, apply business logic, and perform structural modifications.\n",
    "* **Load:** Write the processed dataframe to target storage formats efficiently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Initialize SparkSession\n",
    "Every PySpark application begins with creating a `SparkSession`, which serves as the entry point to programming Spark with the Dataset and DataFrame API."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "from pyspark.sql.functions import col, upper, when, lit, current_timestamp\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize SparkSession\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder \\\n",
    "    .appName(\"Lab5_PySpark_ETL_Pipeline\") \\\n",
    "    .getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Spark Version: {spark.version}\")"
   ]
